Thanks to the help of HJ Lu and Jakub Jelinek, the updated libm has
made it into the CVS tree of glibc [1].  As you may remember, this
libm is based on Intel's libm v2.1 and greatly improves both speed and
accuracy of many routines.  If you'd like to see this libm in your
favorite distro, you may want to let your distributor know, since it's
normally takes some time for distro's to update their libc.

Enjoy,

	--david

